WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:12.354
Hi! In synthesis, you get two sentences and a connector, and you join them into one sentence without changing the meaning. Let's learn the most common ones.

2
00:00:12.504 --> 00:00:22.002
First, although. It was raining. We played outside. This becomes: Although it was raining, we played outside. Don't add but.

3
00:00:22.152 --> 00:00:34.098
Second, so... that. The box was very heavy. I could not lift it. This becomes: The box was so heavy that I could not lift it. Notice very is removed.

4
00:00:34.248 --> 00:00:44.778
Third, too... to. The same two sentences become: The box was too heavy for me to lift. Notice we don't write it at the end.

5
00:00:44.928 --> 00:00:52.458
Unless: If you do not hurry, you will be late becomes Unless you hurry, you will be late. Don't add not after unless.

6
00:00:52.608 --> 00:00:58.986
Despite: She was ill. She went to school becomes Despite being ill, she went to school.

7
00:00:59.136 --> 00:01:08.346
Neither... nor: Tom cannot swim. Amy cannot swim becomes Neither Tom nor Amy can swim. Cannot becomes can.

8
00:01:08.496 --> 00:01:16.338
Always check: does it mean the same as before? Are the punctuation and capital letters correct?

9
00:01:16.488 --> 00:01:20.586
Watch out! Unless you do not study is wrong!

10
00:01:20.736 --> 00:01:27.138
Unless means if not, so it already contains the not. Adding another not flips the meaning.

11
00:01:27.288 --> 00:01:32.466
The correct sentence is: Unless you study, you will fail.

12
00:01:32.616 --> 00:01:44.130
Your turn! The tea was very hot. I could not drink it. Join them with too... to. Pause and think.

13
00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:52.386
The answer is: The tea was too hot for me to drink. No it at the end. Did you get it right?

14
00:01:52.536 --> 00:02:03.474
Another one! Ben was tired. He finished the race. Begin with Despite. Pause and think.

15
00:02:03.624 --> 00:02:10.794
The answer is: Despite being tired, Ben finished the race. Did you get it right?

16
00:02:10.944 --> 00:02:23.202
Here's another! My father does not eat durians. My mother does not eat durians. Begin with Neither. Pause and think.

17
00:02:23.352 --> 00:02:34.698
The answer is: Neither my father nor my mother eats durians. The verb agrees with my mother, the nearer subject, so it's eats. Did you get it right?

18
00:02:34.848 --> 00:02:46.122
One more! You must wear a helmet. If not, you cannot ride. Join them with unless. Pause and think.

19
00:02:46.272 --> 00:02:54.618
The answer is: You cannot ride unless you wear a helmet. No not after unless. Did you get it right?

20
00:02:54.768 --> 00:03:05.850
Remember: when combining, the meaning must stay the same. No but with although, no not after unless, no it at the end of too... to, and cannot becomes can with neither... nor.

21
00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:10.434
Try making a sentence with so... that!

